NAME
    wc - count lines, words, and bytes

SYNOPSIS
    wc [-l] [-w] [-c] [path]

DESCRIPTION
    Counts lines, whitespace-delimited words, and UTF-8 bytes from piped
    standard input, or from [path] inside the shell sandbox when no
    standard input is piped. With no flags, prints all three counts in
    the fixed order lines, words, bytes (followed by [path] when given).

    Lines are counted by splitting on '\n', so a file ending with a
    trailing newline reports one more line than the same text piped with
    its trailing newline stripped.

OPTIONS
    -l  Print the line count.
    -w  Print the word count.
    -c  Print the byte count.

EXAMPLES
    history | wc -l
    wc -l /Logs/notes.txt
    wc /Logs/notes.txt

EXIT STATUS
    0   Counts printed.
    1   Path outside sandbox or file read error.

SEE ALSO
    cat(1), head(1), tail(1), grep(1)
